<title>UNITED NATIONS: U.N. UPDATES IRAQI CONTRACT TOTAL TO SIX APPROVED.</title>
<headline>U.N. UPDATES IRAQI CONTRACT TOTAL TO SIX APPROVED.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Nations has received 17 oil contracts and its oil experts or overseers have approved six of them for a total of 35.02 million barrels, U.N. spokesman Juan-Carlos Brandt said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The six contracts are for the following amounts:</p>
<p>1. 5.5 million barrels</p>
<p>2. 6.12 million barrels</p>
<p>3. 2.7 million barrels</p>
<p>4. 13.5 million barrels</p>
<p>5. 3.6 million barrels</p>
<p>6. 3.6 million barrels</p>
<p>All of the contracts are term deals, though the length and specifications were not released by the U.N.</p>
<p>Of the first six approved, four of the contracts were allocated to Russian, French, Italian and U.S. companies, U.N. sources said.</p>
<p>((United Nations, +1 212 859 1828))</p>
</text>
